.\" Render with: groff -man -Tutf8 smithproxy-privsep.7
.TH SMITHPROXY-PRIVSEP 7 "OCT 2026" "Smithproxy" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
smithproxy-privsep \- Smithproxy privilege separation and communication brokers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smithproxy --run-as nobody
.br
.B SMITHPROXY_RUN_AS=nobody smithproxy
.SH DESCRIPTION
Smithproxy starts its restricted helpers while privileged and then changes the
UID, GID and supplementary groups of the core process. The command-line option
takes precedence over the environment variable. Smithproxy must initially run
as root; starting it directly as the target user cannot create the helpers.
.SH COVERAGE
Privilege separation covers transparent and privileged socket operations,
restricted configuration read/write/backup, PID-file operations, raw GRE
export, CLI and API ingress, and optional webhook network egress.
.PP
Ordinary output files are not delegated. The target user must have filesystem
access to configured logs, captures, TLS key logs and other enabled outputs.
The service manager must prepare communication socket directories and their
ownership before startup.
.SH PRIVILEGED HELPERS
.TP
.B Socket helper
Performs only fixed socket operations: socket creation, selected socket
options, bind and listen. File descriptors pass over a private Unix socket
pair. The helper has no network listener and cannot execute commands.
.TP
.B File helper
Reads, writes and backs up the configured Smithproxy configuration and performs
PID-file operations. Paths are fixed at helper startup. It is not a general
filesystem interface.
.SH COMMUNICATION BROKERS
External brokers may move integration traffic across Unix sockets instead of
giving the core additional network access:
.TP
.BI --comm-gre " path"
Send GRE export packets to an external GRE broker.
.TP
.BI --comm-cli " path"
Receive CLI connections through an external broker.
.TP
.BI --comm-api " path"
Receive API connections through an external broker.
.TP
.BI --comm-webhook " path"
Relay outbound webhook streams through an external broker.
.PP
Without an option, the corresponding standalone/internal transport is used.
Access to each socket is controlled by its filesystem ownership, mode and
parent directory. Communication sockets should not be accessible to untrusted
users.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.nf
    diag sys priv stats
    diag sys gre stats
    diag sys cli stats
    diag sys api stats
    diag sys webhook stats
.fi
.SH SECURITY NOTES
Privilege separation reduces the authority of the Smithproxy core; it does not
configure TPROXY routing, firewall rules or Unix socket permissions. Treat the
configuration, CLI, API, captures and TLS private keys as sensitive data.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smithproxy (1),
.BR smithproxy.cfg (5),
.BR smithproxy-mitm (7)
